# Encryption and key management

## Field-level encryption (Prisma)

- Implemented via prisma-field-encryption with annotations in app/prisma/schema.prisma
- Common patterns:
  - /// @encrypted on PII/financial data (User.email, RegisterEntry.description, AccountRegister.plaidAccessToken, walletAddress, etc.)
  - /// @encryption:hash(field) for deterministic lookup hashes (e.g., plaidIdHash, emailHash)
- Generated migrators:
  - app/prisma/reencrypt/* and microservice/prisma/reencrypt/* expose migrate() to re-encrypt all annotated fields

## Re-encrypt after DB restore

- docs/post-restore-encryption-plan.md describes using generated reencrypt migrate() to convert ciphertext from source env key to local key
- scripts/reset-encrypted-users-after-restore.ts currently provides fallback (placeholder overwrites) and should be extended to use generated migrate when source key is available

## Key rotation (staging automation)

- Staging CronJob (runner-keyrotate image) executes microservice/scripts/k8s-rotate-db-key.sh
  - Rotates DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY/DB_DECRYPTION_KEY_* in ${SECRET_DB}
  - Patches deployments (main + microservice) to roll pods
  - Calls microservice /migrate to re-encrypt with the new key
- RBAC in .deploy/key-rotation-rbac.template.yaml must be applied or granted via IAM (container.roles.*)

## JWT/RSA and related services

- app/server/services/JwtService.ts and RsaService.ts manage JWT secrets/keys and RSA material
- rotateUserJwtKey helper: app/server/lib/rotateUserJwtKey.ts

## Safety notes

- Never log or commit keys; .trufflehog-detectors.yaml enforces scans
- DATABASE_URL and DB_* encryption secrets are intentionally split across different K8S Secrets in templates
- When adding encrypted fields, re-run prisma generate to refresh reencryption migrators
